0..77 Comment "// One builtin of each namespace over its simplest values: negation, division"
78..156 Comment "// and remainder, a list\'s length and element, and string append, equality and"
157..236 Comment "// length. Each is reached by projection from its namespace, which the lowering"
237..315 Comment "// admits for the native primitives alone (#1170) and for no other builtin yet"
316..391 Comment "// (#1106), but where the definition\'s value is first a computation with no"
392..467 Comment "// stated type. Division, append and equality with their types stated check"
468..479 Comment "// and run."
